cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Session Storage Amplification in Long-Horizon Coding Agents: Measurement, Compaction, and a Reference-Based Persistence Architecture"
type: report
authors:
  - name: "Eng Rassam"
date-released: 2026-10-28
version: "1.0"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - coding agents
  - Codex
  - session storage
  - context compaction
  - token accounting
  - storage amplification
abstract: >-
  An empirical study of 52.49 GiB of Codex session rollouts (845 files, January-October 2026).
  Compaction snapshots hold 77.13% of stored bytes and images repeated from the previous
  snapshot 69.34%, while the conversation is 2.89%. Codex's October 2026 rewrite reduces the
  files to 10.60 GiB. Storing images once in a shared media table and referencing them yields
  3.00 GiB with the same zstd level, computed from the pre-October originals; this is a measured
  size ratio under the reported methodology, not an end-to-end production comparison.
